Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Abstract", "Section",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.991336986803117*^9, 
  3.991336988167882*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"80a2c06a-e325-4744-bec0-\
8192ed00df4c"],

Cell["\<\
This Mathematica notebook accompanies the paper Algebraic Structures of the \
Lindblad Equation and presents five worked examples illustrating the \
algebraic formulation of finite-dimensional Lindblad dynamics.

Three examples verify the derived algebraic relations for one-, two-, and \
three-qubit operator bases. The calculations proceed from the construction of \
an orthonormal Hermitian operator basis and its structure constants to the \
associated superoperator algebra. The resulting Liouville superoperators and \
differential equations for the dynamical-map coefficients are compared with \
those obtained by direct construction, confirming their agreement.

Two numerical examples describe transmons truncated to their two and four \
lowest energy levels, including coherent driving, energy relaxation, and pure \
dephasing. They solve the dynamical-map equations and illustrate the \
resulting population dynamics. The four-level example demonstrates an \
approximate X gate and population leakage beyond the computational subspace. \
Both examples construct the unnormalized Choi matrix to check Hermiticity \
preservation, complete positivity, and trace preservation of the computed \
maps. Additional checks in the four-level example examine purely dissipative \
evolution with the Hamiltonian set to zero and unitary evolution with the \
Kossakowski matrix set to zero.

The algebraic construction is parameterized by the number of qubits and \
includes recursion relations for extending it to larger operator bases. \
Although symbolic calculations and storage requirements become demanding as \
the system size increases, the implementation provides a framework that can \
be adapted to other finite-dimensional open quantum systems.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.991337583256125*^9, 3.991337601069256*^9}, 
   4.00187839739779*^9},ExpressionUUID->"8ff21e0d-3bd9-4a3c-94d9-\
129f26870e37"]
}, Open  ]],

